[2C[3A[?2026l]0;⠐ Write 2000-word essay on UNIX history]0;⠂ Write 2000-word essay on UNIX history]0;⠐ Write 2000-word essay on UNIX history[?2026h[2D[3B[4A  In the long arc of computing history, few creations have proved as durable, influential, or quietly revolutionary as UNIX. Born almost by accident in the back rooms of Bell Telephone[K[1B  Laboratories[1Cin[1Cthe[1Clate[1C1960s,[1CUNIX[1Cbegan[1Cas[1Ca[1Cpersonal[1Cproject[1Cpursued[1Cin[1Cstolen[1Chours[1Con[1Ca[1Ccast-off[1Cminicomputer.[1CWithin[1Ctwo[1Cdecades[1Cit[1Chad[1Cbecome[1Cthe[1Clingua[1Cfranca[1Cof[1Cacademic[1B  computer science, the backbone of the burgeoning internet, and the conceptual ancestor of nearly every serious operating system in use today. To understand UNIX is to understand a[K[2C[1Bparticular philosophy of software design — modular, textual,[1Ccomposable,[1Cand[1Cunsentimental[1C—[1Cthat[1Ccontinues[1Cto[1Cshape[1Chow[1Cprogrammers[1Cthink[1Cabout[1Ctheir[1Ccraft[1Cmore[1Cthan[1Chalf[1Ca[1Ccentury
[2Cafter[1Cits[1Cinvention.

